source	J. S. Mill, Utilitarianism (1863), ch. 4
text	Project Gutenberg ebook 11224, https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/11224
class	inference
at	S6	This, however, being a fact
fault	composition: from "each person's happiness is a good to that person" to "the general happiness is a good to the aggregate of all persons" (and "desirable" read as "able to be desired")
reference	G. E. Moore, Principia Ethica (1903), sect. 40; H. Sidgwick, Methods of Ethics, III.xiii
